languagedata===English
;In the languagedata field, enter the language name in that language. Example: ÅgEnglishÅh for English.
;This will appear in the list of language settings within the qwerty3x settings window/screen settings.

languagesetting===en_US
;In the languagesetting field, enter the identifier for this language file.
;There are no naming rules for identifiers. However, identifiers must not be duplicated.
; This file uses the country code & language code to create the identifier,
; but you are not required to follow this naming convention.
; This identifier is not displayed within qwerty3x,
; but it is stored in the configuration file when qwerty3x uses this file.
; The most important point is that Ågthe identifier and the filename (excluding the extension) must be identicalÅh.
;Example: If the identifier is Ågen_USÅh, the filename must be Ågen_US.q3lfÅh.

;Lines starting with Åg;Åh are recognized as comments,
;so they can be used as a memo area.

;Places written as Åg\nÅh are automatically replaced with line break codes internally by qwerty3x.
;Use these for line breaks.

; Parts enclosed in Åg%Åh like Åg%qwertyver%Åh are replaced with variables within qwerty3x.
; Therefore, do not modify the string enclosed within Åg%Åh.

; The structure is Ågidentifier number===stringÅh.
; Do not change the identifier number.

